content.text:
Now write game.js. I'll do it in one big write. Need to be careful with imports.

Imports:
```js
import { W,H,TILE,COLORS,FONT,clamp,rand,randInt,dist,circleRect,hash,OPPOSITE } from './config.js';
import { ROOMS, MAP_CELLS, buildSolid, doorRect, doorTiles, roomSpawn, neighborId, tileCenter } from './world.js';
import { Player, Enemy, Boss, Projectile, Pickup } from './entities.js';
import { drawChest, drawPot, drawSign, drawFlame, drawTorchBracket, drawPickup, drawProjectile, drawParticle, drawKeyIcon, drawBossKeyIcon, drawPixelHeart, drawSparkle, drawEmber, rect, shadow } from './sprites.js';
```

Note `tileCenter` exported as `c` alias; use.

Constants for doors.

Class.

Let's carefully implement.

```js
const DIRS = ['n','e','s','w'];
const DOOR_ORDER = ['n','s','w','e'];
```

Constructor:
```js
this.canvas=canvas; this.ctx=canvas.getContext('2d'); this.input=input; this.audio=audio;
this.time=0; this.mode='title'; this.shake=0; this.hitStop=0; this.flashRed=0; this.flashWhite=0;
this.bgCache=new Map();
this.vignette=this.makeVignette();
this.titleBg=this.makeTitleBg();
this.titleEmbers=...
this.titleTime=0;
this.resetState();
this.mode='title';
```
resetState creates run data but don't enter room? We can call `this.resetRunState()` and set title. Let's have:
```js
resetRunState() {
 this.player = new Player(this, W/2, H-60, 'up');
 this.roomRuntimes = new Map();
 this.doorStates = {};
 ...
 this.roomId='1,2';
 this.roomState=this.getRuntime('1,2');
 this.enemies=[]; this.boss=null;
 this.projectiles=[]; this.pickups=[]; this.particles=[];
 this.visited=new Set(['1,2']);
 this.toast=null; this.message=null; this.reward=null; this.transition=null;
 this.cinematic=0; this.bossBanner=0; this.roomBanner=null;
 this.runTime=0; this.kills=0; this.deaths=0;
 this.deathTimer=0; this.victoryTime=0;
 this.hintTimer=7;
 this.doorHintCooldown=0;
 this.ambientTimer=0;
}
```
But title should have some visuals; resetRunState creates player but no enterRoom. Fine.

`startRun()`:
```js
this.resetRunState();
this.mode='playing';
this.player.x=W/2; this.player.y=H-70; this.player.facing='up';
this.enterRoom('1,2', null, {silent:true});
this.player.x=W/2; this.player.y=H-70;
this.roomBanner={name:ROOMS['1,2'].name,timer:2.6};
this.audio.ensure(); this.audio.startMusic('explore');
this.showToast('Find the two small keys.', 3.5);
```
`enterRoom` with fromDir null uses roomSpawn center; override. It also resets player pos; fine.
But enterRoom may set audio etc.
- `this.audio.startMusic` only once; if already playing explore, reset? startMusic sets nextTime; okay.

`enterRoom(id, fromDir, opts={})`:
- roomId, visited, roomState.
- def.
- spawn = roomSpawn(id, fromDir); player position.
- enemies: if cleared empty else def.enemies map.
- boss: if def.boss && !cleared create boss and push; seal doors; bossBanner, cinematic; setMusic boss. Else boss=null; setMusic explore (unless opts.silent? still).
- projectiles=[], pickups=[].
- roomBanner.
- If def.boss and cleared: door states should be open; ensure.
- `this.transition` unaffected.
- If entering from debug, fromDir.
- Set player.facing = spawn.facing.
- `this.doorStates[id]` exists.

Wait boss door sealing when entering: doorStates['1,1'].n='sealed'; doorStates['1,0'].s='sealed'. But if boss cleared, don't.
- On boss defeat set open.

`getRuntime(id)`.

`spawnEnemyList(id)`.

`circleCollides(x,y,r, ignoreDoors=false)`:
```js
if (x-r < 0 || x+r > W || y-r < 0 || y+r > H) return true;
const solid = buildSolid? cache room.solid
```
Cache solid map per room in `this.solidCache` Map. buildSolid(room).
- tiles:
```js
const tx0=Math.floor((x-r)/16), tx1=Math.floor((x+r)/16), ...
for ... if (solid[y]?.[x] && circleRect(x,y,r,x*16,y*16,16,16)) return true;
```
- pots:
```js
for pot of roomState.pots if !broken && circleRect(x,y,r,pot.x-6,pot.y-6,12,12) return true
```
- chests if !hidden && !? opened still solid; rect x±9,y-7..y+8.
- signs static solid via tile map. Good.
- doors: for each dir, state; rect=doorRect(dir,state); if rect && circleRect(...) return true.
- `ignoreDoors` for projectiles? not needed.
- Dynamic collision with player? no.
- Boss radius 27 may collide with chest in vault? boss room no chest. fine.

`moveBody(body, dx, dy)`:
```js
let blocked=false;
if (dx) { body.x+=dx; if (circleCollides(...)) { body.x-=dx; blocked=true; } }
if (dy) { body.y+=dy; if (...) { body.y-=dy; blocked=true; } }
return blocked;
```
If dx=0 and dy=0, blocked false.

Player radius 6; enemy radius.

Door near:
```js
nearDoor(dir, pad=36) {
 const p=this.player;
 if(dir==='n') return p.x>234&&p.x<278&&p.y<14+pad; // 50
 ...
}
```
Let's define door interior line: north wall bottom y=16; player center must be within y<16+pad. Use pad=22 → y<38. For locked, player stops at y≈20, so yes. For open, transition at y<10.
- s: y>H-38.
- w: x<38 and y 122..166.
- e: x>W-38.
Also require within opening x 238..274 for n/s, y 126..162 for w/e.
- For open transition, use `pastThreshold`: n y<9; s y>H-9; w x<9; e x>W-9. Since player can only reach 6 due to radius. Use <10.
- But when player enters door area from side (x near 256) okay.

`checkDoors()`:
```js
this.doorHintCooldown=Math.max(0,...);
const room=ROOMS[this.roomId];
for (const dir of ['n','s','w','e']) {
 const state=this.doorStates[this.roomId][dir]; if(!state) continue;
 if (this.nearDoor(dir)) {
  if (state==='locked') { if(this.doorHintCooldown<=0) { if(keys>0) unlock else toast; } return; }
  if (state==='boss') { similar; return; }
  if (state==='sealed') { if hint ... return; }
 }
 if (state==='open' && this.pastThreshold(dir)) { this.startTransition(dir); return; }
}
```
