- Check target door exists? not necessary.
- snapshot = document.createElement('canvas'); size W,H; drawScene(sctx) (without HUD). But drawScene applies shake; we can pass `forSnapshot` to skip shake? Simpler set shake=0 before snapshot? Not critical.
- `this.transition={dir,t:0,dur:0.3,snap}`.
- `enterRoom(target,dir)`.
- Note enterRoom sets player position.
- After enterRoom, `this.roomBanner` etc.
- `this.audio.sfx('door')` maybe soft.
- Should we play door sound every transition? Maybe subtle. Add sfx('door') at low? It's 0.38s noise. Could be noisy. Use no sound or quiet step. Skip.

`startTransition` snapshot drawScene uses current player; but `drawScene` uses `this.roomId` etc. Good. It also draws HUD? No, drawScene only world. Good.
- `drawScene` uses `ctx` passed. Ensure no global side effects.

`updatePlaying(dt)`:
```js
this.runTime += dt;
this.hintTimer = max(0,...);
this.doorHintCooldown -= dt;
if (this.roomBanner) { timer-=dt; if<=0 null; }
if (this.bossBanner>0) bossBanner-=dt;
if (this.toast) { timer-=dt; if<=0 null; }
this.flashRed=max(0,flashRed-dt*4);
this.flashWhite=max(0,flashWhite-dt*2);
if (this.transition) { transition.t += dt; if>=dur this.transition=null; this.updateParticles(dt); return; }
if (this.cinematic>0) { this.cinematic-=dt; this.updateAmbient(dt); this.updateParticles(dt); if (this.boss) this.boss.update(dt); return; }
if (this.hitStop>0) { this.hitStop-=dt; return; }
if (this.player.dead) return;
this.player.update(dt);
for (const e of this.enemies) e.update(dt);
this.enemies = this.enemies.filter(e=>!e.dead);
...
```
Careful: boss reference still in enemies; when boss dead, filter removes; this.boss remains but dead. HUD checks boss && !boss.dead.

Order: projectiles update, pickups, particles, ambient, doors, clear.
- Player death could occur in enemy update; if mode changes to dead, continue? Check after enemy loop: if mode!=='playing' return.
- Projectiles can kill player; check mode.
